    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1257">

                <pb facs="1008" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/35.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-11T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 11—11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram of February 6, 6 p.m., and your February 9. Considering the
                    embarrassment with reference to the passage of the troops, the Mexican
                    Government states that it will forego availing itself of the permission granted
                    by the United States. Acting upon the authority granted in the Department’s
                    telegram February 8, 11 a.m., Mexican Government had submitted a request to the
                    Mexican Senate to be permitted to transport troops out of Mexico territory.
                    Mexican Government deems it inadvisable to withdraw from the Senate this
                    request. The action taken will have no significance, but circumstances may arise
                    under which Mexican Government will renew its request.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
